Held;
i.	It is common ground that appeals that do not automatically lie to the Court, may only be preferred with leave or certificate on point of law.
ii.	Certificate on a point of law becomes a requirement when a party intends appeal to the Court for the third time. That is, where the matter originates from the Primary Court a certificate on a point of law is a legal prerequisite under section 5 (2) (c) of the AJA.
